# Workstations in Higher Education.

**Authors:** Weissman, Ronald F. E., And Others

## Abstract
Five articles discuss various aspects of workstations and their applications in higher education. Highlights include microcomputers and workstations; UNIX operating system; campus-wide networks; software; Project SOCRATES and the interdisciplinary aspect of engineering; mechanical system design and simulation; and the Creation Station, a multimedia workstation incorporating music and video. (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ384328

